<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver end weaker in limited trade.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver end weaker in limited trade.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold ended weaker on Tuesday on demand resistance and light profit-taking, dealers said.</p>
<p>Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) fell by 100 rupees to 60,300 rupees per piece. They were up by 400 rupees on Monday. Fears that the customs department might resume sales trimmed early gains, one broker said.</p>
<p>Silver prices ended 15 rupees down from the opening levels. Overall market sentiment was subdued at the close of trade with little demand and prices could react further, they said.  </p>
